{title: Vindicated by Her Children}
{subtitle: Luke 7:24–35}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Bb] | ×4

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]What did you go to the [Bb]wild to see
[C]A reed shaken by the pass[Dm]ing wind
Or a man in soft and [Bb]costly clothes
[C]Those who wear such splendor dwell in [Dm]palaces
But what did you go there to [Bb]find
A [C]prophet, yes, and far more than [Dm]that
Behold, I send my messenger a[Bb]head
Who will pre[C]pare your way before [Dm]you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
No one born of [Bb]women is [C]greater than [Dm]John
Yet the least in the kin[Bb]gdom is [C]greater than [Dm]he
This genera[Bb]tion is like [C]children in the [Dm]square
Calling out to [Bb]one an[C]other in [Dm]vain
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
They sat in the marketplace [Bb]calling out
[C]We played the flute and you [Dm]did not dance
We sang a dirge and you [Bb]did not weep
[C]John came eating no bread [Dm]or wine
You said he has a de[Bb]mon within
[C]The Son of Man came [Dm]eating and drinking
You said a glutton and a drunk[Bb]ard
A [C]friend of tax collectors and [Dm]sinners
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Bb] [C] | ×4
| [Dm] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Tax collectors acknowledged God's [Bb]justice there
[C]For they were baptized [Dm]with John's baptism
But Pharisees rejected God's [Bb]purpose for themselves
[C]Since they had not been bap[Dm]tized by him
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Yet [Bb]wisdom is [C]vindicated by [Dm]all her children
[Bb]Wisdom is [C]vindicated by [Dm]all her [Bb]children
{end_of_verse}

